 It&#x27;s Personnel 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 The SEC charged Jason Satsky , a former BofA utilities banker, with insider trading in South Jersey Industries, ahead of that company announcing an $8.1b takeover agreement with JPMorgan Asset Management. 

 • David Fishman is leaving BofA to join JPMorgan as a vice chair and head of North American tech M&amp;A. He succeeds Vineet Seth , who becomes vice chair of investment banking. axios.link/4ge25G3 

 • Russell Mason joined Moelis &amp; Co. as a managing director of capital structure advisory. He previously was with Houlihan Lokey. axios.link/45JLofy 

 
 
