 Final Numbers 
 
 
 &nbsp; 
 
 Data: PitchBook; Chart: Natalie Breymeyer/Axios The value of biotech reverse mergers is surging, and is unlikely to abate given the deep pipeline of later-stage startups and decaying public shells.

 Abros Therapeutics, a non-opioid pain med startup co-founded by Ohio gubernatorial candidate Vivek Ramaswamy, is the latest example. On Friday it agreed to a reverse merger with Werewolf Therapeutics (Nasdaq: HOWL), after having raised $154m from RA Capital Management, Enavate Sciences, and Italy's Abiogen Pharma. 
 
